---
import { CACHE_CONTROL } from '@/utils/cache-control'
import { SITE_DOMAIN } from '@/utils/meta'
import PageIntro from '@/components/PageIntro.astro'
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

export const prerender = true

Astro.response.headers.set('Cache-Control', CACHE_CONTROL.staticPage)
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How loke.dev and related sites handle infrastructure logs, aggregate analytics events, contact messages, and affiliate click measurement."
  url={`${SITE_DOMAIN}/privacy`}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 md:py-20">
    <PageIntro
      eyebrow="Privacy"
      title="Measure useful actions, not personal browsing profiles."
      description="This notice covers loke.dev and related projects that send aggregate events to loke.dev, including Shuffleworks and FlareCheck."
    />

    <div class="prose prose-invert mt-12 max-w-none">
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 7 August 2026.</p>

      <h2>Who operates these sites</h2>
      <p>
        Loke operates these personal projects from Sweden. Questions,
        objections, and privacy requests can be sent through the <a
          href="/contact">contact page</a
        > or to
        <a href="mailto:hi@loke.dev">hi@loke.dev</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Infrastructure and security logs</h2>
      <p>
        The sites use Cloudflare for hosting, delivery, security, and Worker
        execution. Like other web infrastructure, Cloudflare receives network
        information needed to deliver a request, such as an IP address, user
        agent, requested URL, and security metadata. Some of that information
        may appear temporarily in infrastructure logs according to the
        Cloudflare account settings and retention terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Aggregate site and event analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Loke.dev uses Muro Analytics for basic page-view reporting. Its browser
        script keeps a random visitor ID in local storage for up to 24 hours and
        a random session ID in session storage. These IDs are used to group
        visits, not to identify you by name.
      </p>
      <p>
        Page-view requests may include the page path, referrer, UTM campaign
        values, screen size, device type, browser, operating system, and a
        timestamp. The browser script does not send an email address, account
        ID, advertising identifier, or raw IP address. The analytics endpoint
        can still receive normal network information needed to deliver the
        request.
      </p>
      <p>
        The sites may also use Cloudflare Web Analytics and a separate custom
        event collector for approved actions. Those events can include a site,
        page path, placement, target, campaign label, and count, such as a
        successful command copy, a tool action, a completed shuffle, or an
        outbound partner click. The custom event collector does not set a cookie
        or use local storage.
      </p>

      <h2>Affiliate and outbound links</h2>
      <p>
        Some product links pass through a short loke.dev redirect. The redirect
        records the product and link placement before sending the browser to the
        provider. A commission-capable link is disclosed separately under the
        <a href="/affiliate-disclosure">affiliate and editorial policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact messages and error reports</h2>
      <p>
        A contact message contains the name, email address, and message supplied
        by the sender. Resend processes the email delivery so the message can be
        answered. When error monitoring is configured, Sentry may process
        technical diagnostics needed to investigate failures. Do not put secrets
        or sensitive personal information in a contact message.
      </p>

      <h2>Service providers and external sites</h2>
      <p>
        Current infrastructure and operational providers may include Cloudflare
        for delivery, security, and analytics, Muro Analytics for page-view
        reporting, Sanity for published content, Resend for contact email, and
        Sentry for error diagnostics. Following an external or affiliate link
        makes the destination provider responsible for its own processing under
        its privacy notice.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention and choices</h2>
      <p>
        Aggregate application events are kept only as long as they are useful
        for product and affiliate measurement. Analytics Engine currently has a
        three-month data window when enabled. Muro Analytics retention follows
        the provider's service and account settings. Infrastructure logs follow
        provider and account retention settings. Contact messages are retained
        only as needed to respond, maintain reasonable records, or meet a legal
        obligation.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can block browser analytics requests using browser privacy controls.
        You may also ask about access, correction, deletion, restriction, or
        objection through the contact details above. A request may require
        enough information to locate the relevant record; anonymous aggregate
        events cannot normally be connected back to a particular visitor.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
